{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact group C head 269a6fab1a0fc85c533f2bb478697b0bdd4e960e on planner/docs-paths-c-20261110, all 26 artifacts, for request c33faf23 of documentation request 044311b0 under promise 4019c4d4 and review request d90a03e7. `testing.md`, `self-host.md` and `write-an-application.md` each serve one reader, `deploy.md` opens with the order, `application-views.md` opens with a minimal view, and `check-and-preview-a-package.md` is new.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The splits keep the text. I compared every sentence of the old `testing.md`, `self-host.md`, `deploy.md`, `application-views.md` and `operate-a-service.md` with the 26 changed pages at the head. Apart from headings and sentences whose link now names the new page, each one appears verbatim in a new place. Every code block of the old `testing.md`, `self-host.md`, `write-an-application.md` and `deploy.md` survives. The one deliberate removal is the issue-commitment worked example in `write-an-application.md`, which the Counter and Lending examples replace, as the commit message says.\n- The new prose. I checked about 75 new or rewritten statements against the source. These cover the `dap new`, `dap check` and `dap dev` commands, outputs, flags and refusals in the new page, and the Counter and Lending items, acts, guards and grants in the invariant table. The minimal projection and card in `application-views.md` pass `readApplicationProjection`, `bindApplicationProjection`, `readApplicationViews` and `bindApplicationViews` against the `dap new` definition. Seventy-two hold. The three that do not are listed below.\n- Code references. The comments in `scripts/control.mjs`, `scripts/gate.sh`, `scripts/demo-run.ts` and the Register defect test still point at pages that hold what they cite: `testing.md` still says why there is no mutation sweep, and `deploy.md` still gives the `dap log register --limit 100000` count.\n- The checks. On my own extracted copy of the head, `scripts/check-doc-links.mjs` checks 1,199 local links and finds none broken. `scripts/check-section-citations.mjs` exits 0 with 1,776 resolved and 0 broken.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main 166150ab is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the planner's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 26 paths that its 26 artifacts cover. All are Markdown, and two are package READMEs. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Each long page now has one reader, and the reference material sits on its own pages, linked from the how-to pages.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The change moves and rewrites documents. It drops no security qualification and adds no credential, route or setting.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Three corrections that a later docs head can take:\n\n- `docs/write-an-application.md:185` says each guard of `say` names a refusal reason. The first guard, `{ state: [\"counting\"] }`, names none. The other three name `not-a-player`, `not-your-turn` and `wrong-number`.\n- `docs/application-views.md:120` says `nullable` is `true` exactly when the native slot is not required. For a `fact-signer` field the binding treats the slot as not required, whatever the slot declares (`application-projection-binding.ts:51`).\n- `docs/operate-a-service.md:269` mentions \"the new prepared project\" on a page that assumes the Cloudflare deployment. Link it to the Mac host steps in `self-host-mac.md`.\n\nNo setting changes. This approval authorizes no deployment or publication.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9766f4987e0f97500da102e08a546fd026c4aecf","binding":"assigned","head":"269a6fab1a0fc85c533f2bb478697b0bdd4e960e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a6241c489375eb8c3499ead9367eafdce73772d8\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4019c4d450c3cf0fadeb8303c5cbce8ddecc5f77\"]","review_fronti